course: dictionary
lesson: 5513
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. Leaflet is a good example because it has three meanings: a printed sheet of paper, a small leaf on a plant, and the action of handing out paper sheets.
explain: «Clover leaves usually have three leaflets.» The words clover and leaves are clues. A clover leaf has small parts on it, so leaflet here must mean a small leaf that is part of a bigger leaf. A printed sheet would not fit at all.
explain: «Theo said he'd been at the dentist, but he had no sticker, no leaflet, no numb mouth.» The clues are dentist and sticker, which point to a printed sheet of paper given out at a visit. Try your meaning in the sentence and check that it makes sense.
fact: Many words have more than one meaning, so always check the words around them.
fact: «Leaflet» can mean a small printed sheet of paper, sometimes folded, that gives information or advertises something.
fact: In science, «leaflet» means a small leaf that is part of a bigger leaf.
fact: «Clover leaves usually have three leaflets», and «a horse chestnut leaf is made of five to seven leaflets».
fact: To leaflet an area means to hand out leaflets there.
exercise: «Clover leaves usually have three leaflets.» In this sentence, what is a leaflet? | A small printed sheet of paper | A folded map | A type of flower | *A small leaf that is part of a bigger leaf
exercise: The council will leaflet every house on our street this week. What does leaflet mean here? | To cut down a tree | To count the houses on the street | *To hand out leaflets there | To grow new leaves
exercise: Nadia's leaflet about fire safety told us to check our smoke alarms. What does leaflet mean? | A type of bird | *A small printed sheet of paper with information | A dangerous fire | A small leaf on a plant
test: «The horse chestnut leaf is made of five to seven leaflets like fingers.» What are the leaflets in this sentence? | Fingers | Tiny stones | *Small leaves that are part of one bigger leaf | Pieces of paper
test: «The sensitive plant folds its leaflets within seconds when touched.» What does this sentence tell us about leaflets? | *They are leaves that can fold up quickly | They cannot move at all | They are always printed with words | They are sold in shops
exam: «The sensitive plant folds its leaflets within seconds when touched.» Which meaning of leaflet fits here? | A small bird that sings | *A small leaf that is part of a bigger leaf | A printed sheet of paper that gives information | To hand out sheets of paper to people
